# Phase 15: keeps secrets and irrelevant files out of the Docker BUILD
# CONTEXT entirely (not just out of the final image) — defense in
# depth alongside backend/Dockerfile's own COPY instructions, which
# never reference any of these paths anyway.

# Secrets — never sent to the Docker daemon, let alone baked into an image.
# Patterns here match from the context ROOT only, so every rule that must
# apply in subdirectories (frontend/.env.local, backend/__pycache__, ...)
# needs a **/ form. Fixed 2026-11-26: frontend/.env.local, frontend/
# node_modules, frontend/.next and .venv311 were all in the build context.
# tests/test_dockerignore.py guards these.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Version control
.git
.gitignore

# Python
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.venv/
.venv*/
venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/

# Node: frontend/Dockerfile installs dependencies with `npm ci` and builds
# inside the image; the host's node_modules (macOS binaries) and build
# output must never be copied over them.
**/node_modules/
**/.next/

# Local observability trace files — runtime output, never part of a build
.observability/

# Local data
data/

# Docs and tests are not needed inside the production image
docs/
tests/
*.md

# Local databases used only by local scripts/tests
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite

# Deploy-time files (SSH keys, production env files) never belong in an image
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/prod.env
